+## Deviations from Plan
+
+**1. [Rule 3 - Blocking] `L2Page` gets `verdict` and `l3_inspected` (l2.py)**
+- **Issue:** the hook returns `L2Page` rows and `run_preflight` needs the verdict and the examined count; `l2.py` is not in the plan's file list.
+- **Fix:** two defaulted dataclass fields, no behaviour change for L1 and L2 pages.
+- **Commit:** ff9272b
+
+**2. [Rule 2 - Correctness] Worker also skips L3 when the snapshot has `cloud_allowed` false**
+- Not in the plan text, which only gates on `vlm_detect`. It keeps page images off the wire entirely when the job recorded cloud off (T-03.1-92); the app refuses the same case independently.
+
+**3. Failed pages are omitted, not marked**
+- The plan says an invalid answer "returns that page as failed". `DetectVlmPageResult` requires exactly one of `verdict` or `refused`, and `refused` only has the four guard reasons, so a failed page is absent from `pages`. The worker treats absent as failed. No contract change, so no schema regeneration.
+
+**4. Row layer for L3 pages**
+- Per-page rows report L3 for pages with a verdict; a range still takes the layer of its first page (existing `build_ranges` behaviour, also true for L2), so a fast range that starts on an L1 page and contains an L3 page reports L1 at range level.
+
+## Deferred / notes for later plans
+
+- **Retry of the same attempt:** `rag_parse_budget_reservations` is unique on (job, attempt_no, kind). The hook takes `attempt_no` from its caller; a redelivered job that preflights again with the same number gets a ledger error from `reserve`, the route answers 500, and L3 is skipped for that run (fail-safe, job unaffected). 03.1-40 (worker wiring) should pass an attempt number that does not repeat across redeliveries, or accept this.
+- **Wiring is not done here:** `main.py`'s `/v1/preflight` still calls `run_preflight` without a hook and the worker's `process_job.py`/`tiered.py` belong to 03.1-40. `make_l3_hook(app_client, job_id=..., worker_id=..., attempt_no=..., loop=<worker loop>)` is the entry point; pass the worker's event loop so the shared httpx client is used on its own loop.
+- Batch USD reserved for L3 is not refunded when the model returns nothing usable (no refund function in 0354, same note as 03.1-19).
+- The route's validation failure log (`API validation failed`) is the shared `validateRequest` behaviour and prints zod messages, not values.
